  "body": "## Summary\n\nThe implementation of FOK orders rejects any order where post-lot-rounding a tiny “dust” remainder (>0) remains. Spec says “dust may remain and the order should still succeed so long as the filled amount ≥ requested minus dust,” but code instead does:\n\n```solidity\nif (args.fillOrderType == FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL && newOrder.amount > 0) revert FOKOrderNotFilled();\n```\n\nThus all FOK orders that aren’t exact multiples of lot size now revert, breaking the FOK guarantee.\n\n## Vulnerability Description\n→ Caller posts a FOK buy for `baseAmount = 1.005 × lotSize`.\n\n→ Internal rounding to `floor(amount / lotSize) * lotSize` leaves `0.005 × lotSize` dust.\n\n→  Because `newOrder.amount > 0`, the code does `revert FOKOrderNotFilled()`.\n\n→ According to spec, the order should fill the `1×lot`, ignore the dust, and return success (dust unfilled).\n\n→ Both `_processFillBidOrder` and `_processFillAskOrder` contain the same guard.\n\n```solidity\nfunction _processFillBidOrder(\n        Book storage ds,\n        address account,\n        Order memory newOrder,\n        PostFillOrderArgs memory args\n    ) private returns (PostFillOrderResult memory) {\n        (uint256 totalQuoteSent, uint256 totalBaseReceived) = _matchIncomingBid(ds, newOrder, args.amountIsBase);\n        if (totalQuoteSent == 0 || totalBaseReceived == 0) revert ZeroCostTrade();\n        if (args.fillOrderType == FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL && newOrder.amount > 0) revert FOKOrderNotFilled();\n        // slither-disable-next-line reentrancy-events This external call is to the factory\n        uint256 takerFee = _settleIncomingOrder(ds, account, Side.BUY, totalQuoteSent, totalBaseReceived);\n        emit FillOrderProcessed(\n            CLOBEventNonce.inc(),\n            account,\n            newOrder.id.unwrap(),\n            -totalQuoteSent.toInt256(),\n            totalBaseReceived.toInt256(),\n            takerFee\n        );\n        return PostFillOrderResult(\n            account, newOrder.id.unwrap(), -totalQuoteSent.toInt256(), totalBaseReceived.toInt256(), takerFee\n        );\n    }\n```\n\n```solidity\nfunction _processFillAskOrder(\n        Book storage ds,\n        address account,\n        Order memory newOrder,\n        PostFillOrderArgs memory args\n    ) private returns (PostFillOrderResult memory) {\n        (uint256 quoteReceived, uint256 baseSent) = _matchIncomingAsk(ds, newOrder, args.amountIsBase);\n        if (quoteReceived == 0 || baseSent == 0) revert ZeroCostTrade();\n        if (args.fillOrderType == FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL && newOrder.amount > 0) revert FOKOrderNotFilled();\n        // slither-disable-next-line reentrancy-events This external call is to the factory\n        uint256 takerFee = _settleIncomingOrder(ds, account, Side.SELL, quoteReceived, baseSent);\n        emit FillOrderProcessed(\n            CLOBEventNonce.inc(),\n            account,\n            newOrder.id.unwrap(),\n            quoteReceived.toInt256(),\n            -baseSent.toInt256(),\n            takerFee\n        );\n        return\n            PostFillOrderResult(account, newOrder.id.unwrap(), quoteReceived.toInt256(), -baseSent.toInt256(), takerFee);\n    }\n```\n\n## Impact\nUsers attempting legitimate FOK trades with sizes that are not lot-aligned will always revert, blocking an advertised order type. No value is stolen or locked — just broken functionality.\n\n## Recommendations\nAfter matching completes (inside `_matchIncomingBid/Ask` loops), replace the guard with:\n```solidity\n// we need to allow at most `dust < lotSize`\nif (args.fillOrderType == FILL_OR_KILL && newOrder.amount >= self.settings().lotSizeInBase) {\n    revert FOKOrderNotFilled();\n}\n```",
  "proof_of_concept": "## Proof Of Concept\n\n`forge test --match-test test_submissionValidity`\n\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.27;\n\nimport {PoCTestBase}     from \"./PoCTestBase.t.sol\";\nimport {ICLOB, Side}     from \"contracts/clob/ICLOB.sol\";\nimport {CLOB}            from \"contracts/clob/CLOB.sol\";\nimport {ICLOBManager,\n        SettingsParams}  from \"contracts/clob/ICLOBManager.sol\";\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\ncontract PoC is PoCTestBase {\n    uint256 internal constant LOT_SIZE  = 0.1 ether;\n    uint256 internal constant MIN_BASE  = 0.005 ether;\n    uint256 internal constant MAKER_AMT = 100.2 ether;\n    uint256 internal constant TAKER_AMT = 100.3 ether;\n\n    function test_submissionValidity() public {\n        //\n        // 1) deploy a brand-new CLOB market with (base=tokenA, quote=tokenD)\n        //\n        SettingsParams memory s = SettingsParams({\n            owner:                    address(this),\n            maxLimitsPerTx:          20,\n            minLimitOrderAmountInBase: MIN_BASE,\n            tickSize:                0.0001 ether,\n            lotSizeInBase:           LOT_SIZE\n        });\n\n        vm.prank(address(this)); // our test contract is the \"owner\" for PoCTestBase\n        address fresh = clobManager.createMarket(\n            /* base  = */ address(tokenA),\n            /* quote = */ address(tokenD),\n             s\n        );\n\n        CLOB clob = CLOB(fresh);\n\n        //\n        // 2) seed the book: maker sells 100.2 base @ price=0.1 quote/base\n        //\n        uint256 tick  = clob.getTickSize();\n        uint256 price = tick * 1_000; // 0.1 quote per base\n\n        address maker = makeAddr(\"maker\");\n        vm.startPrank(maker);\n        // mint & deposit base-token so SELL can lock it\n        tokenA.mint(maker, MAKER_AMT);\n        tokenA.approve(address(accountManager), MAKER_AMT);\n        accountManager.deposit(maker, address(tokenA), MAKER_AMT);\n\n        clob.postLimitOrder(\n            maker,\n            ICLOB.PostLimitOrderArgs({\n                amountInBase:    MAKER_AMT,\n                price:           price,\n                cancelTimestamp: 0,\n                side:            Side.SELL,\n                clientOrderId:   1,\n                limitOrderType:  ICLOB.LimitOrderType.GOOD_TILL_CANCELLED\n            })\n        );\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        //\n        // 3) now TAKER tries a FOK buy of 100.3 base → leaves 0.1 dust ⇒ must revert\n        //\n        uint256 quoteNeeded = (TAKER_AMT * price) / 1e18;\n\n        tokenD.mint(address(this), quoteNeeded);\n        tokenD.approve(address(accountManager), quoteNeeded);\n        accountManager.deposit(address(this), address(tokenD), quoteNeeded);\n\n        ICLOB.PostFillOrderArgs memory fArgs = ICLOB.PostFillOrderArgs({\n            amount:        TAKER_AMT,\n            priceLimit:    type(uint256).max,\n            side:          Side.BUY,\n            amountIsBase:  true,\n            fillOrderType: ICLOB.FillOrderType.FILL_OR_KILL\n        });\n\n        vm.expectRevert(bytes4(keccak256(\"FOKOrderNotFilled()\")));\n        clob.postFillOrder(address(this), fArgs);\n    }\n}\n```\n\nLOGS:-\n```bash\nRan 1 test for test/c4-poc/PoC.t.sol:PoC\n[PASS] test_submissionValidity() (gas: 1036990)\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 9.78ms (1.45ms CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 14.17ms (9.78ms CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)\n```",
